1
00:00:14,100 --> 00:00:18,420
Aiming for the setting sun
floating over the Nakagawa,

2
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:23,940
kicking a pebble, I leap off with momentum,

3
00:00:24,480 --> 00:00:29,360
to the kind of guy who
was always clowning around,

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,820
they laughed at me for staying
just as full of energy as ever.

5
00:00:33,820 --> 00:00:38,680
Somewhere, even if I stir up some spirit,
there's only one way to win.

6
00:00:38,680 --> 00:00:43,900
One nightmare, but the unchanging
streets are gentler still.

7
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:49,040
The crows are cawing,
so the day is already fading.

8
00:00:49,680 --> 00:00:53,860
Is yakitori really out there?

9
00:01:05,880 --> 00:01:11,160
Thank you for watching.

10
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:28,920
What the hell is this!

11
00:01:29,260 --> 00:01:30,420
Where the hell is this place!

12
00:01:31,120 --> 00:01:32,440
Are you awake?

13
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:34,660
The model shop, Ozaki's

14
00:01:36,040 --> 00:01:38,080
And the shopping street's

15
00:01:39,540 --> 00:01:41,900
Don't tell me you don't have the money!

16
00:01:42,660 --> 00:01:45,940
We agreed you'd wait on the tab until my bonus,
didn't we!

17
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:48,480
And now you pull a stunt
like this out of nowhere!

18
00:01:50,860 --> 00:01:52,800
No, I'm not here about the tab today.

19
00:01:53,860 --> 00:01:55,840
We need your help, Ryo-san.

20
00:01:55,840 --> 00:01:58,060
My help?

21
00:02:00,360 --> 00:02:02,840
Come on down to the Kameari shopping street!

22
00:02:09,660 --> 00:02:13,580
You want my help? What's this about?

23
00:02:14,080 --> 00:02:15,500
Take a look at this.

24
00:02:17,040 --> 00:02:17,920
What is this?

25
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:21,960
It's Kameari shopping street's
sales for the past few months.

26
00:02:23,860 --> 00:02:27,160
Wow, even Mt. Fuji would be amazed
at how steeply that's dropping.

27
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:29,280
Don't be so carefree about it!

28
00:02:29,700 --> 00:02:31,500
Our livelihoods are on the line here!

29
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:33,420
We know what's causing it.

30
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:34,280
This.

31
00:02:35,280 --> 00:02:37,880
It's the huge shopping mall that
opened in the next town over.

32
00:02:37,880 --> 00:02:41,480
This guy took almost all of our customers.

33
00:02:42,080 --> 00:02:45,160
Because of him,
Kameari shopping street has become deserted,

34
00:02:45,700 --> 00:02:49,860
it's broad daylight, and not even passersby come through.
That's how bad it is.

35
00:02:50,240 --> 00:02:51,600
But it can't be helped, right?

36
00:02:51,600 --> 00:02:58,100
Their prices are lower, and they have a movie theater and a bowling alley,
so it's only natural customers choose them.

37
00:02:58,740 --> 00:03:03,040
I know, I know, but we can't back down here.

38
00:03:04,760 --> 00:03:07,780
Please, Ryo-san, lend us your strength.

39
00:03:07,780 --> 00:03:08,780
Ryo-san.

40
00:03:09,500 --> 00:03:12,280
Bring the customers back
to Kameari shopping street.

41
00:03:13,920 --> 00:03:17,720
That's something you should
handle with your own sales efforts.

42
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:19,660
We've tried all sorts of things.

43
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,240
Handing out flyers,

44
00:03:23,240 --> 00:03:25,040
flying advertising balloons,

45
00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:27,560
but it's had no effect at all.

46
00:03:27,560 --> 00:03:30,300
At this rate,
the shopping street will go under!

47
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:34,100
So what does that have to do with me?

48
00:03:35,520 --> 00:03:39,620
Well, when it comes to business,
it's gotta be Ryo-san.

49
00:03:39,620 --> 00:03:44,260
With power, grit, and ideas,
you've had great success time and again!

50
00:03:44,260 --> 00:03:48,860
We want you to lend that power, grit,
and ideas to the Kameari shopping street.

51
00:03:48,860 --> 00:03:49,961
Please, Ryo-san!

52
00:03:50,011 --> 00:03:53,360
To beat that shopping mall, we have
no choice but to rely on you, Ryo-san!

53
00:03:53,580 --> 00:03:55,380
Help us out!

54
00:03:55,880 --> 00:03:59,200
Even if you say that,
I have work to do too...

55
00:03:59,200 --> 00:04:01,180
I see, that's too bad.

56
00:04:03,060 --> 00:04:04,415
If sales recover,

57
00:04:04,465 --> 00:04:07,120
I was thinking of giving
you a proper thank-you.

58
00:04:07,700 --> 00:04:08,420
Thank-you?

59
00:04:08,820 --> 00:04:11,720
I was going to call all
your past debts even, but...

60
00:04:11,720 --> 00:04:12,700
What!?

61
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:15,800
If sales go up,
I was thinking of giving a bonus.

62
00:04:15,800 --> 00:04:17,980
A bonus?

63
00:04:18,700 --> 00:04:20,060
You idiot!

64
00:04:20,060 --> 00:04:21,860
Why didn't you say so sooner?

65
00:04:21,860 --> 00:04:25,080
Leave everything to
Kankichi Ryotsu's police box.

66
00:04:28,060 --> 00:04:30,340
Secret to business success, number one:

67
00:04:30,340 --> 00:04:32,720
first, we study the enemy.

68
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:35,080
Look into their services and prices.

69
00:04:35,080 --> 00:04:37,400
We need to come up with
services that top theirs,

70
00:04:37,400 --> 00:04:39,060
or we won't win back our customers.

71
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:39,720
I see.

72
00:04:43,920 --> 00:04:45,940
Wow, what an amazing man.

73
00:04:45,940 --> 00:04:47,720
Look at this daikon radish.

74
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:50,960
Everything here is way cheaper
than what the shopping street sells.

75
00:04:52,740 --> 00:04:54,080
That's not all.

76
00:04:54,540 --> 00:04:56,440
Look at how they arrange their products.

77
00:05:03,520 --> 00:05:05,840
Customers keep being
drawn deeper into the store,

78
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:09,320
by putting the loss leaders and
best-sellers up front like that.

79
00:05:13,980 --> 00:05:15,180
Same goes for the electronics.

80
00:05:15,180 --> 00:05:18,220
This VCR, for instance, is less than
half the price of the shopping street!

81
00:05:18,860 --> 00:05:21,300
If they can turn a profit at that price,

82
00:05:21,300 --> 00:05:23,520
their wholesale costs must be really low.

83
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:24,700
That's not all.

84
00:05:26,720 --> 00:05:28,620
By placing competitors
right next to each other,

85
00:05:28,620 --> 00:05:30,160
they're making them
compete against one another.

86
00:05:30,940 --> 00:05:31,300
I see.

87
00:05:31,980 --> 00:05:34,440
Even though they're all
in the same shopping mall,

88
00:05:34,440 --> 00:05:37,340
once they're in business,
they're rivals after all.

89
00:05:38,320 --> 00:05:41,460
Every department is more than 20%
cheaper than the shopping street

90
00:05:42,220 --> 00:05:44,500
This is a tougher rival than I thought.

91
00:05:45,340 --> 00:05:46,620
Don't worry.

92
00:05:46,620 --> 00:05:48,420
Leave everything to me.

93
00:05:48,920 --> 00:05:51,640
Welcome!

94
00:05:55,260 --> 00:05:58,300
This is one way to attract customers too.

95
00:05:59,020 --> 00:05:59,480
I see.

96
00:06:02,820 --> 00:06:04,160
Good morning.

97
00:06:06,740 --> 00:06:09,820
The problem is how to draw in the customers.

98
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:14,920
What's gotten into you today?
Did you eat something weird off the street?

99
00:06:15,020 --> 00:06:16,840
Idiot! I'm in my right mind!

100
00:06:17,880 --> 00:06:21,540
Oh, Nakagawa, I've got something
I want to talk to you about.

101
00:06:22,440 --> 00:06:23,440
Y-yes...

102
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:32,240
General! The time has finally come!

103
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:35,620
to win back our customers
from that hated shopping mall,

104
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:38,280
the moment to rise up has finally arrived!

105
00:06:42,600 --> 00:06:45,460
I've thought up all
sorts of measures for that.

106
00:06:45,460 --> 00:06:48,820
If you do exactly as I say,
not only will business recover,

107
00:06:48,820 --> 00:06:50,920
but success is guaranteed!

108
00:06:54,500 --> 00:06:59,280
So I've decided to start by
reclaiming this shopping street itself.

109
00:06:59,880 --> 00:07:01,280
Take a look at this.

110
00:07:05,100 --> 00:07:07,060
A layout map of the shopping street.

111
00:07:07,060 --> 00:07:10,420
Ryo-san,
the shop locations on this are wrong.

112
00:07:11,720 --> 00:07:20,400
Here, please. Ours is three shops over. No, it's not a mistake.
From today, everyone will move to the locations written here.

113
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:35,720
What do you mean? No, sales vary greatly depending on a shop's location.
So, to ensure fairness, I'm moving the highest-selling shops, in order, to the most prominent spots.

114
00:07:35,720 --> 00:07:41,880
So that means, even though we're fellow members of the same shopping street,
once we're in business, we're rivals.

115
00:07:41,880 --> 00:07:45,080
Just being friendly won't do
the shopping association any good.

116
00:07:45,580 --> 00:07:47,760
Yeah... Shut up.

117
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:54,140
Even important people say it: without reform, there's no growth.
This is already settled.

118
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:11,440
Is this really all right,
doing something like this?

119
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:16,420
This way,
it won't take any trouble to move, right?

120
00:08:16,420 --> 00:08:18,800
If you're frustrated,
just watch your sales go up.

121
00:08:18,800 --> 00:08:20,200
Make an effort to sell more.

122
00:08:24,600 --> 00:08:27,260
The senior shops' relocation is complete.

123
00:08:27,260 --> 00:08:28,420
Alright!

124
00:08:29,080 --> 00:08:31,560
Then, next up is the second
phase of the reform plan.

125
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:37,180
Ryo-san, what is this?

126
00:08:37,180 --> 00:08:38,440
Can't you tell by looking?

127
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:41,800
Old TVs, VCRs, and air conditioners...

128
00:08:41,800 --> 00:08:43,080
No, that's not it.

129
00:08:43,080 --> 00:08:46,700
I'm asking why I was
brought to a place like this.

130
00:08:46,700 --> 00:08:48,020
Isn't it obvious?

131
00:08:48,020 --> 00:08:50,760
From now on, you'll use what's here

132
00:08:50,760 --> 00:08:53,240
to make new products for sale.

133
00:08:53,240 --> 00:08:57,440
Since you can pick your materials from here,
it won't cost any money.

134
00:08:57,440 --> 00:08:59,680
It's the ultimate cost-cutting!

135
00:09:00,100 --> 00:09:00,460
For example,

136
00:09:01,560 --> 00:09:02,980
a TV-style rice cooker,

137
00:09:03,540 --> 00:09:05,720
an air conditioner-style rice cooker,

138
00:09:06,140 --> 00:09:08,440
a washing machine-style rice cooker.

139
00:09:08,440 --> 00:09:10,420
You can't buy things like this anywhere!

140
00:09:11,120 --> 00:09:11,880
Will they sell?

141
00:09:12,440 --> 00:09:14,780
Anyway, original electronics -

142
00:09:14,780 --> 00:09:16,720
make them, make them, mass-produce them!

143
00:09:16,960 --> 00:09:18,680
W-what, that's ridiculous!

144
00:09:23,300 --> 00:09:26,300
R-Ryo-san, let's go home!

145
00:09:26,360 --> 00:09:27,800
We can't take any more of this!

146
00:09:28,020 --> 00:09:28,680
Dumbass!

147
00:09:28,680 --> 00:09:31,320
If we don't catch fish here,
we've got nothing to sell!

148
00:09:31,320 --> 00:09:32,960
B-but...

149
00:09:32,960 --> 00:09:34,480
No more back talk!

150
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:36,220
Catch, catch, and catch some more!

151
00:09:40,480 --> 00:09:41,200
Look.

152
00:09:41,200 --> 00:09:44,560
These are the new costumes
for the Kameari shopping street!

153
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:48,900
From now on,
you'll wear these to serve the customers.

154
00:09:48,900 --> 00:09:51,460
The male customers are sure to line up!

155
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:56,580
You mean we're the ones wearing these?

156
00:09:57,020 --> 00:09:57,620
Hey...

157
00:10:00,280 --> 00:10:01,000
Welcome!

158
00:10:07,100 --> 00:10:08,140
Bagamaan!

159
00:10:08,500 --> 00:10:10,240
Who told you to worry about them?

160
00:10:10,440 --> 00:10:12,100
The part-time girls, that's who!

161
00:10:15,580 --> 00:10:17,220
It's almost finished now, isn't it.

162
00:10:17,680 --> 00:10:19,300
Is this really going to work?

163
00:10:20,180 --> 00:10:22,080
Don't worry! Trust me!

164
00:10:22,340 --> 00:10:25,360
Once this thing is finished,
those people at the shopping mall

165
00:10:25,360 --> 00:10:26,720
are going to be knocked off their feet!

166
00:10:32,020 --> 00:10:33,060
What is this?

167
00:10:36,480 --> 00:10:40,880
What happened? Why aren't any customers coming?
What's going on?

168
00:10:41,460 --> 00:10:43,000
Chief, it's terrible!

169
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:44,280
What is it?

170
00:10:44,280 --> 00:10:48,920
Look at this! The Kameari shopping
street has become a disaster!

171
00:10:48,920 --> 00:10:51,300
What?

172
00:10:51,300 --> 00:10:51,800
What!?

173
00:10:56,340 --> 00:10:59,500
I-I can't believe it!
This is unbelievably cheap!

174
00:11:00,700 --> 00:11:05,900
Welcome!

175
00:11:06,640 --> 00:11:09,800
Cheap, cheap! Everything's 5,000 yen, kids!

176
00:11:09,980 --> 00:11:13,240
Here it is, our shop's original
PC with a built-in fridge!

177
00:11:13,320 --> 00:11:15,826
Now, bundled with a microwave DVD player,

178
00:11:15,876 --> 00:11:17,760
it's a super special price, half off!

179
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:19,480
Ma'am, this is amazing.

180
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:21,220
A cell phone with an earpick attached!

181
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:23,680
This one's a washing machine
that can wash dishes too.

182
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:25,660
Cheaper than anywhere in the neighborhood!

183
00:11:25,660 --> 00:11:26,220
Welcome.

184
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:28,400
Traditional sweets, delicious!

185
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:29,120
Welcome.

186
00:11:29,620 --> 00:11:30,560
A legendary bargain!

187
00:11:30,560 --> 00:11:31,600
Welcome.

188
00:11:33,500 --> 00:11:35,880
No way, that's impossible!

189
00:11:35,880 --> 00:11:38,300
That it's cheaper than ours!

190
00:11:41,260 --> 00:11:43,420
At this rate,
we'll draw in even more customers

191
00:11:43,420 --> 00:11:45,380
and rake in piles of money!

192
00:11:57,820 --> 00:12:00,560
Hi, this is the Wake-Up
Investigation Squad corner!

193
00:12:01,360 --> 00:12:05,360
Today we're at the Kameari shopping street,
the hugely popular spot everyone's talking about.

194
00:12:06,040 --> 00:12:08,900
This shopping street was on the
brink of collapse due to poor business,

195
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:10,940
so how did it bounce back this far?

196
00:12:10,940 --> 00:12:12,880
We'd like to get to the
bottom of that secret.

197
00:12:13,780 --> 00:12:16,620
So, first of all, you planned this renewal,

198
00:12:19,160 --> 00:12:21,900
Ryo-san,
what was the secret to your success?

199
00:12:22,553 --> 00:12:26,340
normally that's a company
secret and I wouldn't answer,

200
00:12:26,340 --> 00:12:29,580
but this time I'll make an exception and tell you.
It's this:

201
00:12:30,680 --> 00:12:32,980
One, a bright smile for everyone.

202
00:12:32,980 --> 00:12:35,220
Two, unyielding sales effort.

203
00:12:35,220 --> 00:12:37,980
Three, answer everyone's hopes,

204
00:12:37,980 --> 00:12:40,260
Four, good goods, truly cheap.

205
00:12:40,260 --> 00:12:42,860
Five, always by your side.

206
00:12:44,760 --> 00:12:49,360
You too, at the Kameari shopping street,
bot-akushu...

207
00:12:54,580 --> 00:12:55,460
This is

208
00:12:55,460 --> 00:12:58,880
I'm in charge of publicity
for our Kameari shopping street.

209
00:12:58,880 --> 00:13:02,600
While protecting world peace and
developing the shopping street,

210
00:13:02,600 --> 00:13:05,180
that's my setting: fighting day and night.

211
00:13:06,240 --> 00:13:09,880
I see, so you're a community-based hero,
the trend these days!

212
00:13:09,880 --> 00:13:14,640
Exactly! We have a different attraction every day,
so nobody gets bored!

213
00:13:14,760 --> 00:13:17,360
A shopping street you'll
want to visit again and again!

214
00:13:17,500 --> 00:13:20,040
This is the eye-catching,
ideal shopping street I've envisioned!

215
00:13:20,340 --> 00:13:21,460
Understood!

216
00:13:21,740 --> 00:13:25,400
Thanks to Ryo-san's
bold and wonderful ideas,

217
00:13:25,400 --> 00:13:28,140
the Kameari shopping street has been reborn,
hasn't it!

218
00:13:28,460 --> 00:13:30,700
And so! To everyone watching on TV,

219
00:13:30,700 --> 00:13:35,920
the Kameari shopping street is eagerly
awaiting your visit today as well!

220
00:13:39,040 --> 00:13:44,540
Ozaki of Plamoya, your shop's sales are last again!
What's going on?

221
00:13:44,540 --> 00:13:48,260
Well, last week I was doing a bit poorly...

222
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:52,420
No excuses!
Plamoya is moving next to the public toilet.

223
00:13:52,900 --> 00:13:57,180
Wait! I'll definitely make up for it this week,
so just a little more time...

224
00:14:00,860 --> 00:14:04,260
The Japanese confectionery and fish shops,
since their sales are up, move beside the plaza.

225
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:05,680
The futon shop stays where it is.

226
00:14:05,680 --> 00:14:08,460
The flower shop and the dried goods shop each move one shop down,
to the end.

227
00:14:09,460 --> 00:14:12,320
Ryo-san, no matter what,
this is going too far.

228
00:14:12,320 --> 00:14:15,080
Exactly,
we sell completely different things.

229
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:19,100
Idiot! Finding a way to make it
work is what a businessman does!

230
00:14:19,100 --> 00:14:22,540
If you want to survive,
use your head a little more.

231
00:14:22,540 --> 00:14:23,560
Understood?

232
00:14:25,100 --> 00:14:26,340
Getting cocky, aren't you?

233
00:14:26,820 --> 00:14:27,780
Acting so high and mighty.

234
00:14:29,180 --> 00:14:29,480
That's the plan.

235
00:14:30,260 --> 00:14:31,120
Well? Answer me!

236
00:14:31,340 --> 00:14:32,780
Yes, understood.

237
00:14:39,900 --> 00:14:43,580
With this, our debts are wiped out,
and then we'll rake in the bonuses.

238
00:14:43,580 --> 00:14:47,480
Yosh! Something's wrong!

239
00:14:48,140 --> 00:14:49,340
What? What happened?

240
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:51,220
Never mind that, just come quick!

241
00:15:01,860 --> 00:15:04,520
What the hell is going on here?

242
00:15:04,520 --> 00:15:08,620
I don't know.
Why did they suddenly disappear?

243
00:15:08,620 --> 00:15:10,360
Ryo-san, I figured it out!

244
00:15:10,780 --> 00:15:12,940
Those guys,
the people from the shopping mall...

245
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:13,900
What?

246
00:15:22,020 --> 00:15:24,680
Come one, come all!
To thank you for your continued patronage,

247
00:15:24,680 --> 00:15:27,020
our Super Blizzard Sale is now on!

248
00:15:27,020 --> 00:15:32,200
Spend 1,000 yen and get one chance at the cash grab,
plus a chance to win your favorite car!

249
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:35,980
A cash grab? Your favorite car?

250
00:15:36,560 --> 00:15:40,960
What are we going to do, Ryo-san? The customers
we finally won back have been taken again!

251
00:15:41,400 --> 00:15:43,680
It's all because Ryo-san let his guard down!

252
00:15:44,140 --> 00:15:48,040
Yeah, just because a few customers came back,
you got cocky, didn't you?

253
00:15:48,040 --> 00:15:50,160
Like it's all my fault or something.

254
00:15:50,160 --> 00:15:56,280
Anyway, at this rate, we'll have to rethink not just the bonuses,
but the plan to wipe out our monthly pay too.

255
00:15:57,020 --> 00:16:00,060
You lot flip-flopped the
second we got into trouble.

256
00:16:00,060 --> 00:16:03,880
Fine, I'll win back the customers,
no matter what.

257
00:16:07,740 --> 00:16:10,420
I said that,
but what the hell are we supposed to do?

258
00:16:11,460 --> 00:16:12,260
Should we just run away?

259
00:16:12,940 --> 00:16:16,160
No, we can't.
If we run away now, I'd lose my manhood.

260
00:16:16,820 --> 00:16:19,680
Not that we have any ideas either.

261
00:16:20,520 --> 00:16:25,120
We can't match them with a raffle, either,
since we can't afford any fancy prizes.

262
00:16:28,020 --> 00:16:28,760
We just don't have any, do we?

263
00:16:38,200 --> 00:16:39,080
This is it.

264
00:16:41,960 --> 00:16:49,180
Why'd you call everyone in like this? You all
want to rebuild this shopping street, right?

265
00:16:49,180 --> 00:16:54,500
Yeah, that's right. Lots of customers
come in and we rake in the cash.

266
00:16:54,500 --> 00:16:57,320
We want a shopping street that makes money,
don't we?

267
00:16:57,860 --> 00:16:59,520
Well, sure, but...

268
00:16:59,520 --> 00:17:02,720
You're prepared to do anything for that,
aren't you?

269
00:17:02,720 --> 00:17:04,480
Why are you making such a big deal of it?

270
00:17:04,480 --> 00:17:06,180
Of course we are.

271
00:17:06,180 --> 00:17:08,500
Good. Don't forget those words.

272
00:17:13,060 --> 00:17:15,040
Here's our next plan.

273
00:17:16,060 --> 00:17:17,540
What is that supposed to be?

274
00:17:17,540 --> 00:17:20,080
That's the same as what
they're doing over there!

275
00:17:20,080 --> 00:17:21,960
Nufufu, how naive.

276
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:25,860
Did you really think I'd make an
ordinary blizzard sale like everyone else?

277
00:17:25,860 --> 00:17:27,760
What do you mean?

278
00:17:27,760 --> 00:17:30,200
Here's what I mean.

279
00:17:33,740 --> 00:17:34,820
When did that happen?

280
00:17:34,820 --> 00:17:38,100
Look, with this lottery machine,
it'll be the talk of the town!

281
00:17:38,100 --> 00:17:40,160
The customers will definitely come back.

282
00:17:40,160 --> 00:17:42,080
B-but that alone isn't enough...

283
00:17:42,560 --> 00:17:45,620
Yeah, you're right, the prizes matter too.

284
00:17:45,620 --> 00:17:48,260
Heh heh heh, I've got everything covered.

285
00:17:48,260 --> 00:17:51,380
We're going with super luxurious
prizes that will beat theirs.

286
00:17:51,960 --> 00:17:53,000
Everyone, lend me your ears!

287
00:17:56,600 --> 00:17:59,200
No way! Who would do something like that!

288
00:17:59,800 --> 00:18:01,980
You said you'd do anything a minute ago!

289
00:18:02,320 --> 00:18:04,240
You'd better keep your promise!

290
00:18:07,620 --> 00:18:10,640
Don't worry! Victory will be ours!

291
00:18:17,080 --> 00:18:17,440
Back again!

292
00:18:19,340 --> 00:18:21,320
Hello, this is the
Amazing Investigation Squad.

293
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:24,060
Today, here at the super
giant lottery machine

294
00:18:24,060 --> 00:18:25,760
the blizzard lottery event is being held.

295
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:27,460
We're here at the Kameari shopping street.

296
00:18:27,940 --> 00:18:29,340
So, right away, once again,

297
00:18:29,340 --> 00:18:30,720
the general producer,

298
00:18:30,720 --> 00:18:33,260
we'd like to ask Mr. Kankichi
Ryotsu a few questions.

299
00:18:33,840 --> 00:18:34,620
Mr. Ryotsu.

300
00:18:34,620 --> 00:18:36,940
You've come up with another outrageous plan,
haven't you?

301
00:18:37,380 --> 00:18:38,100
Of course.

302
00:18:38,100 --> 00:18:39,780
Thinking of the customers

303
00:18:39,780 --> 00:18:41,180
is my duty, after all.

304
00:18:41,660 --> 00:18:42,020
I see.

305
00:18:42,780 --> 00:18:46,680
But some people are saying you just
made the lottery machine bigger.

306
00:18:46,680 --> 00:18:48,160
Nuhahaha!

307
00:18:48,640 --> 00:18:50,000
No need to worry.

308
00:18:51,320 --> 00:18:53,660
What matters most in a lottery,
after all, is the prizes.

309
00:18:53,780 --> 00:18:56,700
We've got some top-notch prizes all ready.

310
00:18:56,940 --> 00:18:59,120
And those prizes are... that!

311
00:19:01,180 --> 00:19:02,641
In this blizzard,

312
00:19:02,691 --> 00:19:05,260
the shop owners will be the balls,

313
00:19:05,380 --> 00:19:06,553
and when one of those balls comes out,

314
00:19:06,603 --> 00:19:10,120
the shop will give away all its goods!

315
00:19:12,340 --> 00:19:14,810
Wow, so it was such a generous promotion!

316
00:19:14,860 --> 00:19:16,400
As expected of Ryo-san!

317
00:19:16,740 --> 00:19:19,520
Kankichi Ryotsu,
a man who gets it done when it counts!

318
00:19:23,060 --> 00:19:27,500
I can't hear you!
Then let's get started right away.

319
00:19:27,500 --> 00:19:30,820
All shop owners,
please get inside the lottery machine.

320
00:19:31,820 --> 00:19:32,900
Stop it!

321
00:19:33,440 --> 00:19:35,060
Just you wait!

322
00:19:36,660 --> 00:19:37,182
Come on,

323
00:19:37,232 --> 00:19:41,240
Now, the Kameari Shopping Street
Super Blizzard Sale begins!

324
00:19:41,660 --> 00:19:43,360
First customer, please come forward.

325
00:19:43,980 --> 00:19:44,960
Yes, thank you very much.

326
00:19:47,560 --> 00:19:49,980
Please, pull that lever.

327
00:19:51,360 --> 00:19:52,180
Together!

328
00:20:03,980 --> 00:20:05,300
What a shame!

329
00:20:05,780 --> 00:20:08,120
We're giving out pocket
tissues and discount coupons.

330
00:20:08,560 --> 00:20:11,280
Okay, next person, come on up to the lever!

331
00:20:14,760 --> 00:20:17,900
Congratulations! Here's your sashimi.

332
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:20,620
There are still plenty of prizes left, so.

333
00:20:23,980 --> 00:20:25,800
Damn, the electrical shop!

334
00:20:26,300 --> 00:20:27,020
Are you all right?

335
00:20:28,640 --> 00:20:30,260
Now it's the ramen shop!

336
00:20:30,700 --> 00:20:32,520
Don't fall! Hang in there!

337
00:20:39,500 --> 00:20:41,900
Why do we have to do something like this?

338
00:20:42,720 --> 00:20:45,460
There's no way I'm letting
Ryo-san get his way like this!

339
00:20:45,460 --> 00:20:48,760
Damn right! We're all going to survive this,
no matter what!

340
00:20:48,760 --> 00:20:49,840
Aaaaaah!

341
00:20:54,940 --> 00:20:57,300
Here's your assorted
sweets and discount coupon.

342
00:20:57,680 --> 00:21:02,080
What's with the
"you get all the store's goods" talk? Nobody's coming out!

343
00:21:02,080 --> 00:21:04,600
Nahaha, sorry about that!

344
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:07,760
Looks like they're determined not to come out,
no matter what.

345
00:21:08,160 --> 00:21:10,360
If nobody comes out,
it's going to look like a scam!

346
00:21:11,840 --> 00:21:15,220
Fine, if that's how it is,
I've got a plan of my own!

347
00:21:17,040 --> 00:21:19,240
Now, reverse-spin chance!

348
00:21:19,240 --> 00:21:21,100
We'll spin it the other way.

349
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:28,040
It's reverse spin!

350
00:21:28,040 --> 00:21:30,160
Don't fall, be careful!

351
00:21:30,620 --> 00:21:33,100
Next, high-speed spin chance!

352
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:35,080
I'll spin it at full speed now.

353
00:21:35,660 --> 00:21:36,520
Stop it!

354
00:21:37,360 --> 00:21:39,500
Damn you, Ryo-san!

355
00:21:40,120 --> 00:21:41,380
I won't lose!

356
00:21:41,380 --> 00:21:43,480
I'll help.

357
00:21:45,240 --> 00:21:47,840
Kunyoku-kunyoku!
Someone hurry up and come out!

358
00:21:47,880 --> 00:21:49,880
If even one of us comes out,
customers will trust us!

359
00:21:50,740 --> 00:21:51,540
Dorya!

360
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:56,440
Damn it, I'll get out no matter what!

361
00:22:02,280 --> 00:22:02,980
Noooo!

362
00:22:12,060 --> 00:22:12,860
Noooo!

363
00:22:19,120 --> 00:22:22,360
All the ramen shop's goods are a jackpot!

364
00:22:23,320 --> 00:22:24,120
Alright, that's it!

365
00:22:26,940 --> 00:22:31,240
Next, the jackpot goes to the weather shop,
the fish shop, and the model shop!

366
00:22:35,900 --> 00:22:37,200
W-what?!

367
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:05,718
Look, the super-large lottery
machine has toppled over, and

368
00:23:05,768 --> 00:23:08,800
Kameari shopping street
has become a city of rubble.

369
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:12,160
N-no way!

370
00:23:12,660 --> 00:23:13,480
Ryo-san!

371
00:23:15,600 --> 00:23:18,200
What are we supposed to do?!
This is a total disaster!

372
00:23:18,500 --> 00:23:21,400
This all started because Ryo-san
came up with something stupid!

373
00:23:21,700 --> 00:23:25,060
That's right! We should have just
done it normally from the start!

374
00:23:25,140 --> 00:23:29,220
What?! You're saying it's all my fault?!
You ungrateful bunch!

375
00:23:29,460 --> 00:23:31,480
Shut up! Securit-ray!

376
00:23:33,280 --> 00:23:35,440
Up until halfway,
things were going fine, weren't they!

377
00:23:35,780 --> 00:23:37,520
Halfway doesn't mean anything!

378
00:23:41,840 --> 00:23:45,240
We're making you pay back
all your past debts, double!

379
00:23:45,660 --> 00:23:46,620
No way!

380
00:23:52,600 --> 00:23:57,940
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling

381
00:23:58,940 --> 00:24:01,840
I walked on, looking back

382
00:24:01,840 --> 00:24:04,480
Led by the hand of the gachapon

383
00:24:05,620 --> 00:24:11,700
That strange feeling I had back then

384
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:16,900
So I walked along the arcade's guide tiles

385
00:24:16,900 --> 00:24:22,680
stepping only on the black ones

386
00:24:25,180 --> 00:24:30,800
Everyone was a child once,
but they've all forgotten

387
00:24:31,920 --> 00:24:38,280
the self-important politicians and
the aunties with blue eyeshadow too

388
00:24:38,760 --> 00:24:43,860
Go on, turn that corner over there

389
00:24:44,920 --> 00:24:49,040
You'll get to see everyone, everyone

390
00:24:49,040 --> 00:24:53,680
Over there is Kame-ari

391
00:24:54,540 --> 00:24:57,020
Surely Kame-ari

392
00:24:58,220 --> 00:25:02,240
Everyone, come on over to our town!

393
00:25:02,240 --> 00:25:06,920
Over there is Kameari,

394
00:25:07,740 --> 00:25:10,160
surely Kameari.

395
00:25:11,100 --> 00:25:15,380
Everyone, come on over to our town!

396
00:25:16,200 --> 00:25:17,000
Thank you.

397
00:25:20,440 --> 00:25:23,820
What? You're putting me in charge
of Chō Kanda Sushi's new branch?

398
00:25:24,040 --> 00:25:26,260
Sounds good, let's do it!

399
00:25:26,260 --> 00:25:29,700
If I win the match against
Matei's big brother, Yuutsu?

400
00:25:29,940 --> 00:25:32,740
Interesting, I'll take on that challenge!

401
00:25:32,740 --> 00:25:37,080
Next time, the Chō Kanda Sushi noren-wake showdown,
see you there!

402
00:25:49,400 --> 00:25:50,800
Thanks.

